\f1\fs22 It was another average morning for Tony: wake-up call at six; cold shower at half-after; breakfast gruel at seven, accompanied by a mug of tea that smelled and tasted like fish had been dying in it; make-up at seven-thirty; green room at eight-thirty; interrogation and torture at nine sharp.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>All the usual tormenters were there: Special Agent Ajent Jones and a cast of henches in ceremonial, identity-hiding hoods; and a full production team and camera crew from 
\f2\i Curb Your Individualism. 
\f1\i0 Of all present, Tony hated the one who seemed most unaffected by his psychological and organic suffering\'97the pasty-faced, frog-eyed best boy electric.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>It was another average morning at 9:04am. At 9:05, recording was halted by the sounds of explosions. The walls of Truth shook. The far end of the studio crumbled; over the rubble lumbered a tank, and aimed its gun barrel at the director\'92s chair.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As angry as Special Agent Jones was, he followed his colleagues in fleeing the scene; as did all of the 
\f2\i Curb
\f1\i0  team, except for the camera operator, kept framing and recording.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The turret hatch of the tank clanged open and an Elvi emerged, wearing what appeared to be a camouflage poncho, with matching cape. \'91Good morning, Mr Tony, sir. I\'92m Specialist 5 Tulsa McLean. In the name of the Holy Momma, we\'92ve come to rescue you.\'92
